I know. We are setting up a reward.

540
00:32:46,940 --> 00:32:48,930
Someone's gonna win a nice prize.

541
00:32:49,030 --> 00:32:50,650
Me! Me! I win the prizes.

542
00:32:50,740 --> 00:32:51,740
Ciccio!

543
00:32:51,820 --> 00:32:52,850
Get your daddy's harpoon!

544
00:32:52,950 --> 00:32:54,660
We're gonna catch a sea monster.

545
00:32:54,740 --> 00:32:55,820
Si!

546
00:32:56,290 --> 00:32:58,450
Sto imbecille thinks he can be a jerk

547
00:32:58,540 --> 00:32:59,600
'cause he keeps winning the race, 

548
00:32:59,620 --> 00:33:01,180
which he shouldn't even
get to do anymore, 

549
00:33:01,210 --> 00:33:03,330
'cause he's too old
and too much of a jerk!

550
00:33:04,670 --> 00:33:06,130
You know, we underdogs

551
00:33:06,210 --> 00:33:07,770
have to look out for each other, right?

552
00:33:08,090 --> 00:33:09,130
What's under the dogs?

553
00:33:09,590 --> 00:33:10,590
Underdogs.

554
00:33:10,680 --> 00:33:12,140
You know, kids who are different, 

555
00:33:12,220 --> 00:33:13,220
dressed weird, 

556
00:33:13,300 --> 00:33:15,510
or a little sweatier than average.

557
00:33:15,600 --> 00:33:16,680
Uh...

558
00:33:16,770 --> 00:33:18,350
Too much? Too much.

559
00:33:18,680 --> 00:33:20,710
So, are you in town for the race?

560
00:33:22,230 --> 00:33:23,640
The portorosso cup?

561
00:33:25,530 --> 00:33:27,070
Well, good talk.

562
00:33:27,360 --> 00:33:30,570
I gotta deliver these.
Always be training, you know?

563
00:33:31,950 --> 00:33:34,660
We should ask her
about this portorosso cup race.

564
00:33:34,740 --> 00:33:37,440
That's how the loud scary human said
he got his Vespa.

565
00:33:38,830 --> 00:33:39,830
Giulial

566
00:33:39,910 --> 00:33:42,240
oh!

567
00:33:42,330 --> 00:33:43,490
- Uh, grazie.
- Ciao.

568
00:33:43,580 --> 00:33:44,690
Hey, uh, spewlia?

569
00:33:44,790 --> 00:33:46,900
Giulia. My name is giulia.

570
00:33:47,380 --> 00:33:51,380
Okay. When you race in a cup, 
what do you get?

571
00:33:52,130 --> 00:33:53,870
Soldi. Prize money.

572
00:33:54,220 --> 00:33:55,220
Oh.

573
00:33:55,300 --> 00:33:56,300
Okay.

574
00:33:56,390 --> 00:33:58,130
- No, no! Keep going!
- What? Why?

575
00:33:58,220 --> 00:33:59,280
Ask her about the prize money!

576
00:33:59,310 --> 00:34:00,350
But that stuff is useless.

577
00:34:00,430 --> 00:34:02,070
- Maybe that becomes a Vespa.
- How does that become...

578
00:34:02,100 --> 00:34:03,460
- Just ask her!
- Fine, fine, fine.

579
00:34:03,810 --> 00:34:05,510
- Hello again.
- Ciao.

580
00:34:05,610 --> 00:34:08,400
Can we turn the money into something else?

581
00:34:08,989 --> 00:34:10,730
- Something like...
- That.

582
00:34:11,900 --> 00:34:14,480
Pfft. No. But it could get you that.

583
00:34:27,960 --> 00:34:29,040
Both: Whoo-hoo!

584
00:34:29,630 --> 00:34:30,630
It's so beautiful.

585
00:34:30,719 --> 00:34:32,050
Yes, we need it.

586
00:34:32,130 --> 00:34:33,830
Great, so we'll just win the race.

587
00:34:35,340 --> 00:34:36,540
You'll have to beat ercole.

588
00:34:36,719 --> 00:34:38,080
Okay, so we'll beat ercole.

589
00:34:38,179 --> 00:34:39,469
Huh. Really?

590
00:34:39,560 --> 00:34:41,520
Thinks he'll beat ercole, 
this guy.

591
00:34:41,600 --> 00:34:43,210
First of all, get in line!

592
00:34:43,310 --> 00:34:46,800
Every summer, that jerk
makes my life miserable.

593
00:34:46,900 --> 00:34:49,730
So, no one's taking him down
unless it's me!

594
00:34:50,780 --> 00:34:52,739
Second, this isn't any old race.

595
00:34:53,239 --> 00:34:56,030
It's an epic, grueling, 
traditional Italian triathlon.

596
00:34:56,120 --> 00:34:58,950
Swimming, cycling, and eating pasta.

597
00:34:59,200 --> 00:35:00,240
So, you'd need a teammate.

598
00:35:00,330 --> 00:35:02,990
Well, we'll figure it out.
Thanks, human girl.

599
00:35:04,670 --> 00:35:07,330
Hey, hey, wait. Wait, Alberto.

600
00:35:07,840 --> 00:35:09,170
What if we join her team?

601
00:35:09,250 --> 00:35:10,350
Giulia: Grazie! Arrivederci!

602
00:35:10,380 --> 00:35:12,000
Hmm. Better idea.

603
00:35:12,090 --> 00:35:13,580
Hey, spew... girl!

604
00:35:13,670 --> 00:35:14,750
Santa mozzarella.

605
00:35:14,840 --> 00:35:16,870
Congratulations, you're joining our team.

606
00:35:16,970 --> 00:35:18,840
I race alone.

607
00:35:24,100 --> 00:35:26,460
But we could be under the dogs, too.

608
00:35:26,560 --> 00:35:27,760
Hey, it's okay, Luca.

609
00:35:27,860 --> 00:35:30,230
She'd rather do
the whole race alone again.

610
00:35:30,320 --> 00:35:32,000
Maybe this time
she won't throw up as much.

611
00:35:32,070 --> 00:35:33,480
Uh, hang on.

612
00:35:36,030 --> 00:35:37,990
You wanna be on my team, eh?

613
00:35:38,280 --> 00:35:39,520
Let's see what you got.

614
00:35:45,250 --> 00:35:46,490
All right, try jumping onto it.

615
00:35:47,380 --> 00:35:48,380
No, no, no.

616
00:35:48,460 --> 00:35:50,080
You gotta show it you're the boss!

617
00:35:51,960 --> 00:35:53,490
Santa mozzarella.

618
00:35:53,590 --> 00:35:54,880
- Eyes up.
- Luca: Huh?

619
00:35:54,970 --> 00:35:57,130
Looking down is what's making you fall.

620
00:36:00,050 --> 00:36:01,050
Luca: Whoa.

621
00:36:03,310 --> 00:36:04,680
Whoa. I'm doing it.

622
00:36:06,060 --> 00:36:07,430
So, can we be on the team?

623
00:36:08,850 --> 00:36:09,930
Can you dodge obstacles?

624
00:36:10,020 --> 00:36:11,930
What if an old lady crosses your path?

625
00:36:13,360 --> 00:36:15,950
Can you withstand
passive-aggressive verbal assaults?

626
00:36:16,030 --> 00:36:18,050
"Nice bike, 
number one and number two.

627
00:36:18,070 --> 00:36:19,070
"I was kidding.

628
00:36:19,160 --> 00:36:20,620
"Your bike is a disgrace."

629
00:36:20,990 --> 00:36:22,070
Finally, can you handle

630
00:36:22,160 --> 00:36:24,370
the course's fiendishly difficult terrain?

631
00:36:24,450 --> 00:36:25,810
Silenzio, Bruno.

632
00:36:33,130 --> 00:36:34,130
Hmm.

633
00:36:36,380 --> 00:36:37,790
Stop. What about you?

634
00:36:37,880 --> 00:36:38,960
Can you swim at least?

635
00:36:39,050 --> 00:36:42,880
Yeah, I'm amazingly
bad at swimming.

636
00:36:42,970 --> 00:36:45,330
You can't swim, 
you can barely ride a bike.

637
00:36:46,890 --> 00:36:48,670
I mean, where are you even from?

638
00:36:48,770 --> 00:36:50,180
We're not telling you our secrets!

639
00:36:50,270 --> 00:36:52,050
- We're runaways.
- Runaways?

640
00:36:52,150 --> 00:36:53,480
I don't know, ragazzi...

641
00:36:54,150 --> 00:36:55,150
Please?

642
00:36:55,440 --> 00:36:57,930
My family was gonna send me
somewhere horrible.

643
00:36:58,030 --> 00:36:59,860
Away from everything I love.

644
00:37:00,030 --> 00:37:02,400
But if we win this race, well, 

645
00:37:02,490 --> 00:37:03,850
we can be free.

646
00:37:04,950 --> 00:37:06,980
My life's great. I'm just helping him out.

647
00:37:07,080 --> 00:37:08,200
Hmm.

648
00:37:08,290 --> 00:37:09,750
Just give me one more chance.

649
00:37:10,250 --> 00:37:11,250
No.

650
00:37:11,880 --> 00:37:13,590
You guys want it just as bad as I do.

651
00:37:13,670 --> 00:37:14,670
You have the hunger.

652
00:37:14,750 --> 00:37:16,030
That's the most important thing.

653
00:37:16,130 --> 00:37:17,470
I'm definitely hungry.

654
00:37:17,550 --> 00:37:20,340
Perfetto! You eat, you bike, and I swim.

655
00:37:20,430 --> 00:37:22,720
Giulia: Underdogs?

656
00:37:23,680 --> 00:37:24,970
Alberto and Luca: Underdogs.

657
00:37:25,390 --> 00:37:27,630
Now we just need money for the entry fee.

658
00:37:27,810 --> 00:37:29,100
From my dad.

659
00:37:38,570 --> 00:37:41,660
All right, just let me do the talking
and act casual.

660
00:37:41,740 --> 00:37:43,200
He doesn't do well with fear.

661
00:37:43,280 --> 00:37:44,730
Hey, papa! I brought

662
00:37:44,830 --> 00:37:46,270
some friends for dinner.

663
00:37:46,290 --> 00:37:47,970
Is there enough for four?

664
00:37:50,660 --> 00:37:51,820
“Whoa.

665
00:37:51,920 --> 00:37:53,660
What's wrong with you, stu...

666
00:38:01,340 --> 00:38:02,920
What do you think he kills with those?

667
00:38:03,890 --> 00:38:06,260
Massimo: Anything that swims.

668
00:38:06,350 --> 00:38:08,060
Hai visto il giornale today?

669
00:38:08,140 --> 00:38:10,180
That photo is a fake, papa.

670
00:38:10,850 --> 00:38:14,090
Everyone in portorosso
pretends to believe in sea monsters.

671
00:38:14,610 --> 00:38:16,520
Alberto: Huh.

672
00:38:16,610 --> 00:38:18,690
Massimo: Well, I'm not pretending.

673
00:38:20,690 --> 00:38:21,890
Huh?

674
00:38:32,370 --> 00:38:33,700
Slipped.

675
00:38:35,460 --> 00:38:36,460
En.

676
00:38:37,880 --> 00:38:38,920
Both: Phew!

677
00:38:41,840 --> 00:38:42,950
Massimo: Dinner's ready.

678
00:38:43,380 --> 00:38:44,990
Trenette al Pesto.

679
00:39:08,200 --> 00:39:09,280
Mmm!

680
00:39:13,250 --> 00:39:14,250
Uh...

681
00:39:14,920 --> 00:39:15,920
Luca: Mmm!

682
00:39:17,250 --> 00:39:18,250
Okay.

683
00:39:19,710 --> 00:39:22,160
Where did you boys say you were from?

684
00:39:24,050 --> 00:39:26,590
They're, uh, 
classmates. From genova.

685
00:39:26,680 --> 00:39:28,390
Luca and, uh...

686
00:39:28,470 --> 00:39:30,310
Alberto. Alberto.

687
00:39:31,020 --> 00:39:33,510
And what brings you to portorosso?

688
00:39:33,600 --> 00:39:34,680
Giulia: Oh. Uh...

689
00:39:34,770 --> 00:39:36,060
Funny you should ask.

690
00:39:36,150 --> 00:39:37,360
They came for the race.

691
00:39:38,020 --> 00:39:39,100
The race?

692
00:39:39,270 --> 00:39:40,470
Yeah.

693
00:39:40,570 --> 00:39:43,190
Uh, you know what? Don't worry about it.

694
00:39:43,280 --> 00:39:44,940
"Don't worry about it"?

695
00:39:45,530 --> 00:39:47,520
Mm-hmm. Don't worry about it.

696
00:39:47,620 --> 00:39:50,780
Massimo: Giulietta. A word.

697
00:39:52,580 --> 00:39:54,490
I don't want you doing the race again.

698
00:39:54,580 --> 00:39:55,740
You get so upset.

699
00:39:55,830 --> 00:39:58,280
Papa, per favore, I have a team now.

700
00:39:58,380 --> 00:40:01,370
There's also the entry fee.
Money is tight.

701
00:40:01,460 --> 00:40:03,640
I'll work double shifts at the pescheria.
Whatever you need.

702
00:40:03,670 --> 00:40:06,000
I can't sell what I don't have.

703
00:40:06,090 --> 00:40:08,420
What I need is more fish in my net.

704
00:40:10,800 --> 00:40:12,410
Luca: Um, excuse me?

705
00:40:12,510 --> 00:40:13,870
We could help.

706
00:40:13,970 --> 00:40:15,380
You know fish?

707
00:40:15,480 --> 00:40:17,310
Oh, we? We know lots of fish.

708
00:40:17,390 --> 00:40:19,550
- Massimo: Huh.
- Can this face lose?

709
00:40:21,440 --> 00:40:24,280
You want to work? I'll put you to work.

710
00:40:24,360 --> 00:40:25,850
Really?

711
00:40:25,950 --> 00:40:27,660
Oh, grazie, papa.

712
00:40:30,910 --> 00:40:33,150
Machiavelli! Don't you...

713
00:40:33,240 --> 00:40:35,650
No! Machiavelli!

714
00:40:38,080 --> 00:40:39,780
I'm so sorry about the cat.

715
00:40:39,880 --> 00:40:41,370
I don't know what got into him.

716
00:40:41,460 --> 00:40:44,330
It's fine. We're gonna head back to, uh...

717
00:40:44,880 --> 00:40:45,880
Ohl

718
00:40:45,970 --> 00:40:48,590
do you guys need a place to stay?

719
00:40:50,340 --> 00:40:51,340
Cool.

720
00:40:51,430 --> 00:40:53,840
Oops! Sorry. This is my...

721
00:40:53,930 --> 00:40:54,930
Your hideout.

722
00:40:55,350 --> 00:40:57,690
Huh. Yeah. My hideout.

723
00:40:57,850 --> 00:40:59,760
Buonanotte, boys.

724
00:41:00,310 --> 00:41:01,310
Whoa!

725
00:41:02,610 --> 00:41:05,320
Slipped.
Uh, see you in the morning.

726
00:41:07,360 --> 00:41:08,850
- That was close.
- I know.

727
00:41:08,950 --> 00:41:10,780
Like, how big was that dad human?

728
00:41:10,860 --> 00:41:12,350
That guy kills things, for sure.

729
00:41:12,450 --> 00:41:14,350
I thought we were gonna die, 
like, a hundred times.

730
00:41:14,370 --> 00:41:15,370
Hey, relax.

731
00:41:15,450 --> 00:41:17,190
We're incredible at this humaning stuff.

732
00:41:17,290 --> 00:41:19,160
Yeah. You're right.

733
00:41:19,250 --> 00:41:20,580
Did you see me on the bike?

734
00:41:20,670 --> 00:41:21,790
Giulia said, "look up, "

735
00:41:21,880 --> 00:41:23,270
and then all of a sudden, I was riding it.

736
00:41:23,290 --> 00:41:24,770
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
Our Vespa's gonna be

737
00:41:24,840 --> 00:41:26,580
even better than a bike, though.

738
00:41:26,670 --> 00:41:29,030
Because the moment we get it, 
we're outta here.

739
00:41:31,050 --> 00:41:33,660
I can't wait.

740
00:41:50,070 --> 00:41:51,530
How could my mother tell him

741
00:41:51,610 --> 00:41:53,720
about this town of bloodthirsty lunatics?

742
00:41:53,820 --> 00:41:55,900
I still can't believe he would do this.

743
00:41:55,990 --> 00:41:56,990
It's not like him.

744
00:41:57,080 --> 00:41:58,240
Just keep your guard up.

745
00:41:58,330 --> 00:42:00,010
There's gonna be land monsters everywhere.

746
00:42:01,620 --> 00:42:04,580
- Daniela! Ooh! Wait! Ow! Ow!
- No! Not today, land monster!

747
00:42:04,670 --> 00:42:06,160
- It's me!
- Oh!

748
00:42:06,250 --> 00:42:07,740
You scared the scales off of me!

749
00:42:07,840 --> 00:42:09,130
Jeez, you're strong!

750
00:42:09,210 --> 00:42:10,560
I'm sorry, I'm just a little on edge.

751
00:42:10,590 --> 00:42:13,500
No. I needed that. It really woke me up.

752
00:42:13,680 --> 00:42:16,510
Wow! We look horrifying.

753
00:42:16,600 --> 00:42:18,060
Ugh, gross.

754
00:42:18,140 --> 00:42:19,930
Come on. Let's find our son.

755
00:42:36,200 --> 00:42:39,070
Oh, no! Oh, no!
Alberto! Wake up!

756
00:42:39,160 --> 00:42:40,990
What? Ahh! The sky's been leaking!

757
00:42:54,220 --> 00:42:56,090
Hmm. Uh...

758
00:42:56,180 --> 00:42:57,420
Oh. There you are!

759
00:42:57,720 --> 00:42:59,250
Buongiorno.

760
00:42:59,350 --> 00:43:00,470
All right, ragazzi.

761
00:43:00,560 --> 00:43:02,520
You want that entry fee, 
you got to earn it.

762
00:43:02,600 --> 00:43:03,640
- Giulietta...
- I'm on it!

763
00:43:03,690 --> 00:43:06,060
- You make the deliveries.
- Already makin' 'em! Ciao!

764
00:43:06,150 --> 00:43:08,230
Hmm. You two are coming with me.

765
00:43:08,320 --> 00:43:09,320
Luca: Oh.

766
00:43:09,400 --> 00:43:11,190
Which knife do I get? Huh? Huh?

767
00:43:11,280 --> 00:43:12,570
You don't.

768
00:43:14,360 --> 00:43:15,720
Tommaso: Buongiorno, massimo!

769
00:43:15,820 --> 00:43:18,400
You'll keep an eye out
for those sea monsters, right?

770
00:43:18,490 --> 00:43:19,850
We're all counting on you.

771
00:43:19,950 --> 00:43:22,980
Don't worry, tommaso.
I've got my eyes peeled.

772
00:43:23,080 --> 00:43:24,490
They won't get away.

773
00:43:33,840 --> 00:43:35,870
Hey, this isn't a joyride.

774
00:43:35,970 --> 00:43:37,380
Make yourselves useful.

775
00:43:44,640 --> 00:43:45,640
Uh...

776
00:43:50,440 --> 00:43:52,690
Massimo: Hey, 
no goofing around back there.

777
00:44:14,880 --> 00:44:16,490
A sea monster ate it.

778
00:44:16,880 --> 00:44:17,990
Huh? What?

779
00:44:18,510 --> 00:44:22,510
Ma, no.
This is how I came into the world.

780
00:44:27,900 --> 00:44:28,900
Whoa.

781
00:44:28,980 --> 00:44:31,650
Mannaggia, not a great catch today.

782
00:44:31,730 --> 00:44:35,180
It might be because we're
over a haunted fish graveyard.

783
00:44:35,280 --> 00:44:38,150
We know it's not haunted.
The fish think it's haunted.

784
00:44:38,240 --> 00:44:41,910
This time of day, most fish
will be right about there.

785
00:44:43,200 --> 00:44:44,310
Massimo: Hmm.

786
00:44:46,120 --> 00:44:47,570
Both: Ciao, giulia.
Giulia: Ciao.

787
00:44:50,000 --> 00:44:51,160
Ha-ha!

788
00:44:51,250 --> 00:44:52,530
New personal best!

789
00:44:53,000 --> 00:44:54,990
Santo pecorino.

790
00:44:55,090 --> 00:44:56,300
Alberto: Shoo! Shoo!

791
00:44:58,430 --> 00:45:00,890
Your friends do know fish.

792
00:45:01,140 --> 00:45:03,850
Benissimo!
Ooh, let's go sign up.

793
00:45:10,850 --> 00:45:11,880
Okay. Okay.

794
00:45:11,980 --> 00:45:13,820
Now, what's our plan? Think, Daniela.

795
00:45:13,900 --> 00:45:15,860
Hey, everything's always on you.

796
00:45:15,940 --> 00:45:17,180
I wanna step up.

797
00:45:17,280 --> 00:45:20,990
- Uh... you sure?
- Oh, yeah. I got this.

798
00:45:22,870 --> 00:45:25,200
Oh, hello there, young man.

799
00:45:25,290 --> 00:45:27,200
- You're not fooling anyone.
- Lorenzo, eh-eh.

800
00:45:27,290 --> 00:45:29,330
Did you really think
you could get away with this?

801
00:45:29,410 --> 00:45:31,520
- Renzo...
- You thought we wouldn't find you?

802
00:45:31,630 --> 00:45:32,940
- Well, guess what?
- I don't think...

803
00:45:32,960 --> 00:45:34,800
